  <prompt><![CDATA[
The `EntityLookupConfig` interface (currently declared at
`src/client/pcf/AssociationResolver/handlers/RecordSelectionHandler.ts:37`) is
consumed by callers that need to pass through the metadata value from
`sprk_recordtype_ref.sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield`. Task SRFR-022 relocates
the surrounding `FieldMappingHandler` into `@spaarke/ui-components`; the
`EntityLookupConfig` interface itself will move as part of that migration OR
in this task (whichever lands first).

This task adds one optional property: `regardingRecordNumberField?: string`.
It is the source-field name on the target entity from
`sprk_recordtype_ref.sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield`. Task SRFR-020
(PolymorphicResolverService extension) and task SRFR-050 (AssociationResolver
dynamic config loader) will populate + consume this property. This is the
interface portion of FR-B4-01.
  ]]></prompt>

  <role>TypeScript interface engineer familiar with the Spaarke shared component library, backward-compatible interface extension, and the ADR-012 public-surface boundary.</role>

  <goal><![CDATA[
`EntityLookupConfig` carries the new optional property
`regardingRecordNumberField?: string` at its canonical location. If the
interface has already moved into `@spaarke/ui-components` (task 022 landed
first), it is exported from `src/index.ts`; if not, it remains in-place and
gets picked up by task 022 in the same release. All existing callers still
compile without modification because the addition is a non-breaking optional
property.
  ]]></goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="spec">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="plan">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/plan.md</file>
    <file purpose="project-claude">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    <file purpose="source-if-not-yet-moved">src/client/pcf/AssociationResolver/handlers/RecordSelectionHandler.ts</file>
    <file purpose="destination-if-moved">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/</file>
    <file purpose="public-surface">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts</file>
    <file purpose="consumer">src/client/pcf/AssociationResolver/AssociationResolverApp.tsx</file>
    <file purpose="adr">.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-component-library.md</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Shared type MUST be exported via the public surface path (`src/index.ts`) when it resides in the shared lib. No subpath imports.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-B4-01">Interface addition is OPTIONAL — `regardingRecordNumberField?: string`. MUST NOT break existing callers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Type name unchanged (`EntityLookupConfig`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Property name is `regardingRecordNumberField` (camelCase, matching TypeScript convention). It carries the LOGICAL name of the source field on the target entity (e.g., `sprk_matternumber`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Backward-compatible extension only. No renamed properties, no removed properties.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">TypeScript strict mode preserved. No `any`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>shared-lib/interface-extension</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-component-library.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Non-breaking optional extension" location=".claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-component-library.md">
        Adding an optional property (`?:`) is safe for existing callers because absence
        satisfies the type. New callers gain the ability to pass the value; old callers
        continue to compile and behave unchanged.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <context>
    <background>
      The Field Mapping subsystem uses `EntityLookupConfig` to describe per-entity lookup
      behavior in the AssociationResolver. With FR-A4-01 introducing data-driven record-number
      resolution (task 020), the config shape needs an optional slot to carry the source-field
      name discovered from `sprk_recordtype_ref.sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield`. This task is
      a minimal, focused interface addition. It coordinates with task 022 (relocation) and 020
      (consumer) so the whole change lands in the `@spaarke/ui-components` minor release per A-05.
    </background>
    <dependencies></dependencies>
    <related-work>
      <item>Task SRFR-022 relocates the surrounding FieldMappingHandler + likely this interface.</item>
      <item>Task SRFR-020 consumes the property when writing the 5-field payload.</item>
      <item>Task SRFR-050 (Wave 5) populates the property via dynamic config loader over `sprk_recordtype_ref`.</item>
    </related-work>
  </context>

  <steps>
    <step order="0" name="Context Check">Verify context &lt; 60%. Read spec.md FR-B4-01. Read the current `EntityLookupConfig` declaration.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Locate the Interface">Grep to determine whether task 022 has already landed. If interface is in `@spaarke/ui-components/src/services/`, extend there. Otherwise extend in `src/client/pcf/AssociationResolver/handlers/RecordSelectionHandler.ts:37`.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Add Optional Property">Add `regardingRecordNumberField?: string;` with a JSDoc comment stating: "Source-field logical name on the target entity, from sprk_recordtype_ref.sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield. When set, the resolver reads this field on the target record and writes to the host's sprk_regardingrecordnumber column."</step>
    <step order="3" name="Update Public Surface (if applicable)">If interface resides in the shared lib, ensure `EntityLookupConfig` is exported from `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts`. If already exported, no-op.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify Backward Compat">Compile `AssociationResolverApp.tsx` and confirm the file at `src/client/pcf/AssociationResolver/AssociationResolverApp.tsx:44` (the current import site) still compiles unchanged.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Verify Presence">Run `grep -R "regardingRecordNumberField" src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components` (or in the PCF path if not yet moved) and confirm the interface definition appears.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Build">Run `npm run build` in the package(s) containing the interface. Fix any TS strict errors.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Step 9.5 Quality Gate">Invoke `/code-review` and `/adr-check` on the changed file. Confirm ADR-012 public-surface rules satisfied.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Update Task Status">Update TASK-INDEX.md 🔲 → ✅ for SRFR-023. Reset current-task.md for next task.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="Read">Load the current interface + consumer file</tool>
    <tool name="Grep">Locate the interface + confirm presence after change</tool>
    <tool name="Edit">Add the optional property + optional `src/index.ts` export</tool>
    <tool name="Bash">Run `npm run build` in the affected package</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Extended `EntityLookupConfig` interface (path depends on whether task 022 landed first)</output>
    <output type="code" conditional="if-in-shared-lib">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts (public export confirmed)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/set-regarding-and-field-mapping-resolver-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md (🔲 → ✅ for SRFR-023)</output>
  </outputs>

